  - Kept 6 nested surface islands together as one hollow shell. Auto Axis and every
    fracture plane are shared by the outer and inner walls so generated caps connect
    them instead of closing the cavity separately.
  - 21 cut segment(s) could not be chained within the normal weld tolerance; affected
    caps preserved their real edge order and closed the final numerical seam.
  - Intact collision uses 4 compound parts. In Whole Building modular workflow each
    authored panel keeps its own Hollow Shell collider instead of one convex hull
    spanning the room interior.
  - 4 rectangular modular wall/floor collider(s) use oriented BoxColliders with the
    authored Hollow Shell thickness. No triangulated collider surface is stored for
    those panels; irregular modules keep the convex-mesh fallback.
  - Whole Building combined 8 coplanar modular panel seam(s) into continuous wall/floor
    colliders and support groups. Corners and real gaps remain separate.
  - 'Large Whole Building defers inactive fragment physics: only pieces that actually
    detach receive a Rigidbody. This keeps a local first break from registering all
    250 pieces with PhysX.'
